<BlogPost title={title} description={description} publishDate={publishDate} category={category} relatedTools={relatedTools} locale="en">

<div class="lead">
  <p>I tested over 30 "free" PDF tools online. Most add watermarks, have hidden fees, or require sign-ups that spam your inbox.</p>
  <p>Here are the 5 tools that actually deliver on their promise - truly free, no catches, and they work brilliantly.</p>
</div>

<section>
  <h2>1. Compress PDF - Best for Reducing File Size</h2>
  <p><strong>What it does:</strong> Reduces PDF file size by up to 90% without quality loss</p>
  <p><strong>Why it's great:</strong> Most compression tools either don't compress enough or destroy image quality. Our <a href="/en/tools/compress-pdf/">compress tool</a> offers three compression levels - you can optimize for quality OR file size depending on your needs.</p>
  <p><strong>Best use case:</strong> Email attachments that exceed size limits</p>
  <p><strong>Truly free?</strong> Yes - no watermarks, no file limits beyond 50MB, completely free</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>2. Merge PDF - Best for Combining Documents</h2>
  <p><strong>What it does:</strong> Combines multiple PDF files into one document</p>
  <p><strong>Why it's great:</strong> Drag-and-drop reordering makes it dead simple to arrange files exactly how you want them. Plus, you can merge up to 20 files at once - most free tools cap at 2-3 files.</p>
  <p><strong>Best use case:</strong> Creating complete reports from separate sections, job applications with multiple documents</p>
  <p><strong>Truly free?</strong> Yes - up to 20 files, 100MB total, zero watermarks</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>3. PDF to JPG - Best for Image Extraction</h2>
  <p><strong>What it does:</strong> Converts PDF pages to high-quality JPG images</p>
  <p><strong>Why it's great:</strong> Outputs at 300 DPI (professional quality) while most free converters max out at 150 DPI. You can convert all pages or select specific ones - super flexible.</p>
  <p><strong>Best use case:</strong> Extracting images for presentations, social media sharing, website content</p>
  <p><strong>Truly free?</strong> Yes - unlimited conversions, download as individual files or ZIP</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>4. Split PDF - Best for Page Separation</h2>
  <p><strong>What it does:</strong> Separates a PDF into individual pages or extracts specific page ranges</p>
  <p><strong>Why it's great:</strong> Two modes - "split all pages" creates separate PDFs for each page, or "extract range" pulls specific pages (e.g., 1-5, 10, 15). Most tools only offer one or the other.</p>
  <p><strong>Best use case:</strong> Extracting one page from a large document, removing unnecessary pages</p>
  <p><strong>Truly free?</strong> Yes - works with PDFs up to 500 pages</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>5. Rotate PDF - Best for Orientation Fixes</h2>
  <p><strong>What it does:</strong> Rotates PDF pages 90°, 180°, or 270° clockwise</p>
  <p><strong>Why it's great:</strong> Scanned documents often come out sideways. This tool fixes orientation instantly without re-scanning or compromising quality.</p>
  <p><strong>Best use case:</strong> Fixing scanned documents, correcting landscape pages</p>
  <p><strong>Truly free?</strong> Yes - no page limits, instant processing</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Honorable Mentions</h2>

  <h3>JPG to PDF</h3>
  <p>Converts images to PDF format. Perfect for creating PDFs from phone photos or scanned images.</p>

  <h3>Extract Pages</h3>
  <p>Similar to Split PDF but keeps extracted pages in one PDF instead of separate files.</p>

  <h3>Remove PDF Password</h3>
  <p>Unlocks password-protected PDFs (you need to know the password). Essential for working with secured documents you own.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Why These Tools Stand Out</h2>

  <h3>1. Actually Free</h3>
  <p>No hidden costs, no watermarks, no "upgrade now" popups. These tools do exactly what they promise.</p>

  <h3>2. Privacy-First</h3>
  <p>All processing happens in your browser using JavaScript. Your files never leave your device - critical for sensitive business documents.</p>

  <h3>3. No Sign-Up Required</h3>
  <p>No email capture, no account creation, no spam. Just open the tool, use it, and move on with your day.</p>

  <h3>4. Mobile-Friendly</h3>
  <p>Works perfectly on phones and tablets. Upload from your camera roll, process, and download - all from your mobile device.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>When to Use Paid Tools</h2>
  <p>These free tools handle 95% of everyday PDF tasks. Consider Adobe Acrobat Pro ($14.99/month) if you need:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Advanced editing (adding text, images, signatures to existing PDFs)</li>
    <li>OCR for scanned documents (making scanned text searchable)</li>
    <li>Batch processing (handling hundreds of files automatically)</li>
    <li>Form creation and data extraction</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Final Verdict</h2>
  <p>After testing dozens of tools, I keep coming back to these five. They're reliable, genuinely free, and respect your privacy.</p>
  <p>Bookmark this page - you'll need these tools more often than you think!</p>
</section>

</BlogPost>